Local Character

Optional creature armatures use the UniRig skeleton model from VAST-AI Research
and the GPL-3.0 ComfyUI-UniRig inference implementation by PozzettiAndrea,
pinned to 69ee59dc459d2da7cb0291930c1f944886c31d7c. The external provider keeps
its original source and GPL license, with small standalone Torch/SDPA adaptations;
no ComfyUI server or Blender Python package is required for inference.
The safetensors conversion from apozz/UniRig-safetensors is pinned separately
and derives from the MIT-licensed VAST-AI/UniRig model release. Both upstream
license notices are retained. Checkpoints stay external and are not bundled.
Rigmodo's job transport, Blender armature construction and UI integration are
independently authored. See unirig-lock.json and docs/creature-rigging.md.

Optional Pose from Image uses SAM 3D Body and DINOv3 as separate local providers.
SAM sources/checkpoints are governed by Meta's SAM License, not this extension's
GPL. Provider installation retains their licenses in the external cache; images
are processed locally. Rigmodo's image-pose interchange and retargeter are
independently authored. See docs/image-pose-implementation.md and upstream
https://github.com/facebookresearch/sam-3d-body/blob/main/LICENSE.

soma30.json contains the SOMA-30 skeleton definitions from NVIDIA Kimodo,
distributed under Apache License 2.0, and the parent-local rest offsets
distributed by localai-org/kimodo.cpp at revision
5679ff19ba0a522c0b0516e9a9d402fe1af2c027 under Apache License 2.0.
The root offset is zero: generated root positions already include hip height.
See licenses/Apache-2.0.txt.

External inference code, native binaries, model checkpoints and Python
dependencies are installed separately in the LocalCharacter provider cache.
Their individual license texts and notices remain with those components.
kimodo.cpp uses ggml, copyright the ggml authors.
The independently authored Local Character key-pose entry point is Apache-2.0
licensed and distributed with corresponding source/notices in the native ZIP.
It exposes the pinned port's existing conditioned sampler; upstream sources
and the original unconstrained executable remain unchanged.

Kimodo's text encoder is based on Meta Llama 3: Built with Meta Llama 3.
Its weights are subject to the Meta Llama 3 Community License and acceptable
use policy. The SOMA motion weights use the NVIDIA Open Model License.
These model licenses do not become GPL by use with this extension.

The original Make-It-Animatable model code is MIT licensed. Its models_ae.py
derives from 1zb/3DShape2VecSet, MIT licensed. The selected original MIA
checkpoint model card identifies its weights as Apache-2.0. Neither ARP nor
the original Blender, UI, dataset or pose modules are imported by our adapter.

Optional Creature Motion runs Friedrich-M/UniMate at revision
b78c7807df7cf4231d4e67f8d0ece29c5e11025b (MIT) as an external provider.
The released Linzhan/UniMate checkpoint is CC BY-NC 4.0, not GPL;
this optional integration is for noncommercial use. The FLAN-T5 text encoder
is Apache-2.0. Weights, dataset assets and external runtimes are not bundled.
No UniML3D dataset, commercial Truebones files, cloud LLM or API token is needed.
Canonicalization, FK recovery and conditioning adapt the MIT-licensed
UniMate-B3D addon/motion.py and backend/worker.py by nopeburger, with changes
for Rigmodo's transactions, validation, offline setup and owned workers.
Upstream: https://github.com/Friedrich-M/UniMate
Blender reference: https://github.com/nopeburger/UniMate-B3D

